From f439868b95d656e4d94bdd8582b69a757a39e216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mattia Tadini <info@mtsistemi.it>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:07:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sched_ext: keep scx_bpf_error_bstr() in BTF when built with
 gcc -O3 -march=znver2

Built with gcc -O3 -march=znver2 (the SkillFishOS BC-250 kernel), vmlinux
BTF lacks scx_bpf_error_bstr() and sched_ext fails to initialize:

  sched_ext: Failed to register kfunc sets (-22)

resolve_btfids warns "no BTF func for kfunc scx_bpf_error_bstr in
scx_kfunc_ids_any". gcc describes @data__sz only as DW_OP_reg6 (RBP), the
callee-saved register the prologue moves it to, not as RDX, the register it
arrives in, and pahole (1.31 and 1.32 alike) drops the function as having
an unexpected parameter register. The same source built for generic x86-64,
or at -O2, is not affected.

Keep @data__sz in memory with barrier_data(), the same workaround as
upstream commit f2f095c87603 ("sched_ext: Work around pahole 1.32 dropping
scx_bpf_task_set_lazy_resched() from BTF"). Checked on build_policy.o with
gcc 16, -O3 -march=znver2: all four parameters now start in their argument
registers, and pahole emits the function.

Signed-off-by: Mattia Tadini <info@mtsistemi.it>
---
 kernel/sched/ext/ext.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c b/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c
index 84774147a..3e953836b 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c
@@ -10241,6 +10241,13 @@ __bpf_kfunc void scx_bpf_error_bstr(char *fmt, unsigned long long *data,
 {
 	struct scx_sched *sch;
 
+	/*
+	 * gcc -O3 -march=znver2 describes @data__sz only in the callee-saved
+	 * register the prologue moves it to, so pahole drops this kfunc from
+	 * BTF and sched_ext fails to register its kfunc sets (-EINVAL). Keep
+	 * @data__sz in memory so its location names no register.
+	 */
+	barrier_data(&data__sz);
 	guard(rcu)();
 
 	sch = scx_prog_sched(aux);
-- 
2.55.0

